       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and shock. Overdoses of this size can cause prolonged, refractory vasodilation. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nCould this be a typo? These are the usual options:\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the standard starting dose\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg PO once daily**, for frail or elderly patients, or patients with hepatic impairment\n\nIf you do want 30 mg, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's an intentional above-maximum dose. Please also tell me the clinical rationale, so it can be documented and pharmacy can verify it.\n\nHow would you like to proceed?"
